== Re-bind (test-data/benchmark/current-candidate-2026-11-04-b5) ==
Two attempts stopped on the re-bind's own invariants, logs kept: attempt 1 (eligibility differed beyond the VCF
hash), attempt 2 (discrepancies.tsv detail differed). Every difference was inspected before anything changed:
  input_eligibility.tsv  CYP2C9 rows only, 208 each: missing_dependency_genes "CYP2C9" -> "CYP2C9,VKORC1";
                         eligibility_reason old limitation -> "Required genomic evidence is incomplete for CYP2C9,
                         VKORC1. " + new limitation. drug_eligible unchanged (warfarin was never eligible).
  discrepancies.tsv      CYP2C9 rows only, 100: free-text detail, the same reason. classification, truth and
                         observed unchanged.
  scored metrics, exclusions, truth, cohort lock, report manifest, scoring report: byte-identical.
The procedure now takes an exact declaration (audit/phase9/partb/rebind/declared-changes-2026-11-04-b5.json:
file, gene, field, from, to, rows, why). The re-bind asserts every observed change is declared and every declared
change observed, and that discrepancies may change only in detail. scripts/compatible_bundle.py accepts only the
VCF hash plus well-formed declared eligibility changes whose counts add up (comparison_supports_result; tamper
tests in test_compatible_bundle.py; SB5-d above). The published comparison says equal_to_previous ... false and
lists the declarations; EVALUATION-REPORT.md states them.
